                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "27c0b595-453e-35da-bb51-e8f11c8fe74d",
                        "entry_id": "0f8e9447-7cdf-3e41-84b1-e71e2dc069b8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of a river, water, etc.: to flood or flow into (a place)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3eeb0846-56c7-4ac7-bd77-5688edff0727",
                                "sense_id": "27c0b595-453e-35da-bb51-e8f11c8fe74d",
                                "text": "But O—Alas! 'twas in thy native town, / Franklin, they strove to crush the hero down; / Revil'd and stamp'd him with the stain of blood, / That he in battle should the foe inflood!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "93331f74-db15-4127-b18e-ea75b5894494",
                                "sense_id": "27c0b595-453e-35da-bb51-e8f11c8fe74d",
                                "text": "An officer (Capt. Baker) has been despatched to Gharra, with a view to forward the arrangements for a canal between that place and the Indus; […] This is to have the effect of inflooding the country below Shahapore, and returning the blessing of fresh water to the lands which formerly enjoyed it, and which are in the possession of a faithful ally."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "502cc3ef-f24b-4b2a-908e-2522a10166ac",
                                "sense_id": "27c0b595-453e-35da-bb51-e8f11c8fe74d",
                                "text": "Because of the divine abundance inflooding our souls, there's an important truth for us to remember: To enable us to carry out His will, God is always ready to give us more than enough of Himself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad60870a-3feb-40a2-a2d7-6e8650c0f46e",
                                "sense_id": "27c0b595-453e-35da-bb51-e8f11c8fe74d",
                                "text": "In an unpublished letter addressed to [Russell] Cheney on November 20, 1924, [Francis Otto] Matthiessen associates the affective excess inflooding their relationship with the contradictory temporal logics that his specter straddled: […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "824c9ca3-c3a8-333a-af76-939e33cf911f",
                        "entry_id": "0f8e9447-7cdf-3e41-84b1-e71e2dc069b8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To flood or flow in; to inflow."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f494ad22-50db-4710-8edf-9edc6568c016",
                                "sense_id": "824c9ca3-c3a8-333a-af76-939e33cf911f",
                                "text": "[T]hough remote / From the main ocean many a mile / Inflooded past cape, creek, and kyle, / The sea-loch flanked by precipice walls, / With ever-lessening murmur crawls, / Till 'neath the Pass he lies subdued / By the o'er-aweing solitude; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "22aa1c25-2e91-43ac-94b5-fda502d08bac",
                                "sense_id": "824c9ca3-c3a8-333a-af76-939e33cf911f",
                                "text": "Joy, from the light inflooding upon eye and mind, / And heart and soul, calm bliss without care's harsh alloy, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb2c52fe-70a7-4aec-86aa-e271fc1b5053",
                                "sense_id": "824c9ca3-c3a8-333a-af76-939e33cf911f",
                                "text": "[…] Evelyn Underhill said there is a place in every person's mind that is this gateway—the gateway through which things inflood rather than outgo."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
